        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0292" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg196"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United states</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2916.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my dispatch No. 2901½, of the 2d
                    instant, I set out the terms of a settlement of the recent riot at Chiang Pei
                    which I had agreed on with the Tsung-li Yamên.</p>
                <p>One of the stipulations was the payment of 500 taels as damages. This amount had
                    been wired me by the consul-general as the sum recommended by our consul at
                    Chung king, but it turned out that there was a telegraphic error, and that the
                    true sum was 5,000 taels. I informed the Yamên of the mistake and demanded the
                    latter sum.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
